That package contains software derived from TimesFM
(https://github.com/google-research/timesfm), Copyright 2026 Google LLC, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its licence therefore differs from the rest
of this repository and is recorded per-package; see LICENSE-Apache-2.0.

Changes to the derived work, as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b):

  - The inference path is translated from Python/PyTorch to C#/TorchSharp: the
    patch embedding residual block, the mixing transformer stack (sequence
    attention, variate attention, feed-forward), the quantile output head, and
    the preprocessing around them — cumulative running statistics, RevIN,
    future-covariate rolling and the wrap mask.
  - Training, fine-tuning, batching APIs, the decode cache and iterative CPM
    RevIN refinement are not ported.
  - Attention runs through TorchSharp's scaled_dot_product_attention, which has
    no scale override. The reference leaves rescale_logits false and so produces
    logits of QK^T * sqrt(d); the query is pre-scaled here so the fixed
    1/sqrt(d) division yields the same result.

No Google source files are redistributed. scripts/fetch-timesfm-reference.sh
retrieves them at a pinned revision, for parity checking only.

